Chapter 10
Currency: what moves a rate, and what a move costs
العملات: ما الذي يحرك سعر الصرف وما الذي يكلفه تغيره
Orontes sells tahini in four countries and buys equipment from two. Every one of those transactions is agreed in one currency and settled in another, and between the agreement and the settlement the rate moves. This chapter is about that gap.
It covers four things: how an exchange rate works its way into the price of a good, which is where the exposure starts; what makes rates move, which is the part candidates most often reduce to a list; how to compute an appreciation or a depreciation and say which way it ran; and what a movement costs, in the accounts and in the business. Chapter 11 then manages the exposure.
Figure F810-01 is your map.
Figure F810-01. Chapter 10 roadmap: rates and prices, what moves them, measuring the move, and what it costs.
